# Testing Rules

- Add unit tests for services and tools.
- JeffyMCP tool tests live under `tests/JeffyMCP/JeffyMCP.Tests/` (mirror `src/JeffyMCP/`).
- JeffyGPT MCP client / executor tests live under `tests/JeffyGPT/JeffyGPT.Application.Tests/Tools/`.
- When adding a JeffyMCP tool, follow the checklist in `tool-calling.mdc` (JeffyMCP unit test; optional executor/orchestrator coverage when chat flow changes).
- Prefer integration tests for API endpoints.
- Use test names that describe behavior (`Method_Scenario_Expected`).
- Application.Tests folders: `Chat/` (orchestrator, validators, stream events), `Infrastructure/` (OpenAI client, DI), `Tools/` (executor/MCP/policy), one `TestDoubles/` at the project root.
- Do not depend on a live LLM in normal automated tests.
- Mock or fake the LLM client behind `IAssistantClient`.
- API tests should not spawn a real MCP subprocess — use `TestMcpToolBootstrapper` / disable configured servers (see `JeffyGPTWebApplicationFactory`).
- Frontend predicate tests live beside the module under `JeffyGPT.Web/src/` and run with `npm test` (Vitest).

## Test projects

| Project | Focus |
|---------|-------|
| `JeffyGPT.Application.Tests` | Orchestrator, validators, tool executor, MCP catalog doubles |
| `JeffyGPT.Api.Tests` | HTTP endpoints via `WebApplicationFactory<Program>` |
| `JeffyMCP.Tests` | JeffyMCP tools + FileSystemSandbox |

Run from repo root: `dotnet test`
